# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this static HTML project.

## Changes Made

### Modified Files:

1. **site/index.html** - Added Vercel Analytics script tag
2. **site/privacy.html** - Added Vercel Analytics script tag
3. **site/terms.html** - Added Vercel Analytics script tag
4. **site/vercel.json** - Updated Content Security Policy to allow analytics

## Implementation Details

### Analytics Script
Added the following script tag to the `<head>` section of all HTML pages:
```html
<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>
```

This implements Vercel Web Analytics using the CDN method, which is the recommended approach for static HTML sites without npm/build tooling.

### Content Security Policy Updates
Updated the CSP headers in `vercel.json` to allow:
- `script-src`: Added `https://cdn.vercel-insights.com` to allow loading the analytics script
- `connect-src`: Added `https://vitals.vercel-insights.com` to allow sending analytics data

## Why This Approach

This project is a vanilla JavaScript static site without a package.json or build process. According to the official Vercel documentation, the recommended method for such projects is to:

1. Add the analytics script tag via CDN: `<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>`
2. Update the Content Security Policy to allow the script and data endpoints

This approach:
- Requires no package installation or build process
- Works immediately upon deployment to Vercel
- Automatically tracks page views and Web Vitals
- Is non-blocking (uses `defer` attribute)

## Next Steps

After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings > Analytics)
2. Verify analytics are working by checking the Network tab for requests to `vitals.vercel-insights.com`
3. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after traffic accumulates

## References

- Vercel Web Analytics Quickstart: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Vercel Analytics Package Documentation: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/package
- Implementation based on official Vercel documentation retrieved October 1, 2026
